# Build context for container/flock-ocr/Dockerfile: deny by default, then admit
# only the hash lock and top-level engine wheel files. Docker applies the last
# matching rule, and a rule also matches every path below a matching directory,
# so each admitted name is followed by a recursive re-exclusion of anything
# nested under it. tests/test_flock_ocr_container.py exercises these semantics.
*
dist/**
!requirements.lock
!dist/deflock_campaign_tool-*-py3-none-any.whl
requirements.lock/**
dist/*/**
